dsh-jingshen 0.4.1 · 精神

This is an independently adapted personal plugin, not an official DeepSeek product.
It incorporates code from deepseek-ai/dsh-superagent-prototype under the MIT license.
Upstream snapshot: 8c32a9dc5d72c033816c6a8110b37f40cf94fba4
Upstream URL: https://github.com/deepseek-ai/dsh-superagent-prototype
The upstream LICENSE is included unchanged.

The personal bundle reuses the upstream transactional Engine, SQLite Store and
Effects queue. Necessary upstream source and migration assets are included in
upstream/; PROVENANCE.json records small Harness API and asset-path adaptations.
Conversation delivery, delegation and session-local model selection use DeepSeek Harness 0.2.2-rc.5.
The GitHub/Feishu watchers, team setup, team prompts and upstream management UI are not mounted.

The interpretation of Hegel and the new experience, memory, runtime and UI code belong
to this adaptation. No claim is made that the software literally has consciousness,
reproduces the philosophical necessity of the Phenomenology, or attains absolute knowing.

Live vision uses the Apache-2.0 MediaPipe Tasks runtime and TensorFlow's
EfficientDet-Lite0 detector. The detector, its attribution and its license are
in src/vision-assets/. Character artwork was generated for this adaptation
using the visual reference provided by its author.

Xiaoyu's Mandarin speaker reference was generated from original dialogue and
acting directions with Qwen3-TTS VoiceDesign (Apache-2.0). The bundled preview
contains new lines synthesized from this reference by the local call engine.
Sources, checksums and generation settings are in scripts/character-voice/voice.json.
The optional local speech setup downloads the k2-fsa Emilia-trained ZipVoice
Distill model (CC BY-NC) and the Vocos 24 kHz vocoder separately.
Model terms: https://huggingface.co/k2-fsa/ZipVoice#4-license
Vocoder: https://huggingface.co/charactr/vocos-mel-24khz
